Z||000000||Turkey on Rye||11-25-2001||09:25 PM||||Hello Everyone, my name is chris and was wonderin if i could get your help on something.  I have an 86 Fiero Gt with a 2.8 stroked out to a 3.1L  It is a very quick car, but i have a craving for more power.  I have read some post on V-8 Swaps, and even surfed Archies Website, and now i am very intrigued with the idea of a swap.  I was just wondering how much a swap would be TOTAL at the end. I've also heard of the 4.9L caddy swap, is this one cheaper and better?  Any info on this would be wonderful. Thank you all.<BR>                           -Chris ||||reg||1
Z||000001||jeffndebrus||11-25-2001||09:32 PM||||chris, welcome <BR>there is a wealth of info to be found out there. Try using the search funtion on this site to find info.<BR>you can also go to rockcrawls homepage or do a search for the alternative fiero which will take you to bubba joe's site<BR>look up ed parks at the fiero factory in alabama<BR>look up ace engineering<BR>look up design one systems<BR>you already saw archies site<BR>try chris west at west coast fiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Turkey on Rye||11-25-2001||09:35 PM||||ok, thank you very much for the information.  I;ll do some searhcing. Any more info is welcome.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||11-25-2001||10:54 PM||||An Archie swap done right (done by Archie) will set you back $5-8K with a new engine.  Prices will vary all over the place depending on what else needs to be done to make the car road worthy.<P>If you know what you are doing, you can do it for less than that.||||reg||1
Z||000004||joplinfiero||11-25-2001||10:57 PM||||Hi, <P>I am just about half way to a v-8 fiero so I can tell you a little about how much it costs<P>engine-4200<BR>kit-950<BR>starter-165<BR>Clutch-172<BR>tools-600<BR>2 fiero's-1400<BR>misc-250<P><BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||PBJ||11-25-2001||11:04 PM||||Part way through a 4.9 swap, I am budgeting for $1000.00 in parts and am doing the labour myself.  Have a 86 GT to begin with.||||reg||1
