Z||000011||PBJ||11-26-2001||05:56 PM||||an engine replacement with a another 2.8 would be about 10 hrs just to pay for the in and out.<P>A swap for any thing other than what came with the car, you can count on 20 hrs + labour and as for the engine could be $5-600.00 to $5-6000.00.  There is no clear answer on how much and engine swap costs.<P>  Figure how much you have (or want to spend), get a quote for what you want and add half as much again to the quote and that should work.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Daleford||11-27-2001||07:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fastback87:<BR><B>Which modern V8's fit as a direct bolt on to the tranny?  This is the first I have heard of this...Tell me more...Please.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Cadillac 4.1, 4.5, 4.9 all bolt to the Fiero Trans. Do a search here. OOdles of info. [ how do you spell oodles? ]<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
